1
00:00:00,267 --> 00:00:02,933
Once a submarine dives, GPS
is gone.

2
00:00:03,600 --> 00:00:06,967
GPS works by radio, and
seawater soaks up radio

3
00:00:06,967 --> 00:00:10,300
its signals can't reach a
submerged submarine.

4
00:00:10,967 --> 00:00:13,067
So the boat keeps track of
itself.

5
00:00:13,067 --> 00:00:16,500
Gyroscopes sense every turn,
accelerometers sense every

6
00:00:16,500 --> 00:00:19,267
push and pull, and a
computer adds it all up.

7
00:00:19,933 --> 00:00:22,100
The catch: tiny errors add
up too,

8
00:00:22,100 --> 00:00:24,067
and the estimate slowly
drifts.

9
00:00:24,733 --> 00:00:28,233
So every so often it checks
against something outside

10
00:00:28,233 --> 00:00:31,800
for example, coming up near
the surface for a GPS fix,

11
00:00:31,800 --> 00:00:34,467
or matching the seafloor
below to a map.

12
00:00:34,467 --> 00:00:36,967
Methods vary between navies
and boats.

13
00:00:37,633 --> 00:00:40,400
Sense the motion, add it up,
then check it

14
00:00:40,400 --> 00:00:43,633
that's how a submarine finds
its way without GPS.
